<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juliana of Cornillon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1192–<a href="/years/1258">1258</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Juliana of Liège</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juliana of Cornillon was an Augustinian nun near Liège whose visions led her to campaign for a feast honouring the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eucharist">Eucharist</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-of-thourotte">Robert of Thourotte</a> instituted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-christi-feast">Feast of Corpus Christi</a> in the diocese in 1246, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-iv">Pope Urban IV</a> extended it to the whole church in 1264. She is venerated as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juliana-of-cornillon.jpg" alt="Juliana of Cornillon" width="320" height="512" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo: Andreas Praefcke · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Merazhofen_Pfarrkirche_Chorgest%C3%BChl_links_Juliana.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
